 {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
   {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "1. Why do anesthesiologists need specialized malpractice insurance?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "Anesthesiology carries unique risks—handling potent medications, managing airways, and monitoring vital signs under anesthesia. Even rare complications can lead to large claims. Specialized malpractice coverage ensures your personal assets, practice, and career are protected against claims specific to your specialty."
    }
   },
   {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "2. How much does an anesthesiologist malpractice insurance cost?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "Annual premiums typically range from $15,000 to $60,000, depending on factors like your location, practice setting, procedures, claims history, and coverage limits. At Agency Height, we help you compare competitive quotes from top-rated insurance professionals to find coverage that fits your needs and budget."
    }
   },
   {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "3. How can I reduce my malpractice premiums?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "Good risk management can lower costs. This includes completing approved risk courses, maintaining thorough documentation, ensuring informed consent, and practicing clear communication with patients and surgical teams. Our agents guide you on risk management strategies that can help reduce your exposure and premiums."
    }
   }
  ]
